            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0949" n="938" xml:id="pg938"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390D.11/79</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steger</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 316</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-09">November 9, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        24.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 312 of November 3, 1937, reporting the verbal assurances given by the French
                    High Commission with regard to recognition of the nationality of American
                    citizens of Syrian and Lebanese origin, and to enclose a copy, with translation,
                    of the High Commission’s note dated November 5, 1937, which repeats these
                    assurances in writing.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Christian T.
                    Steger</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d731-a1.xml" xpointer="d731-a1"/>
